    "concern_summary": "Lead Purchase vs Seller Listing Mismatch",
    "resolution_sop": "1. Verify customer identity. Ask for registered name, company name, and mobile number. Confirm the transaction amount and time. 2. Ask the customer to log in or guide them to log in. Say: Go to Seller Dashboard > Payments > Transactions. 3. In Transactions, locate the \u20b9470 entry. Click View Details. 4. Check transaction type. If it shows 'Single Lead' or 'Buyer Details', tell the customer this payment bought one buyer lead. 5. Navigate to My Requirements or Enquiries. Click the listed requirement. If the customer did not intend to post a requirement, click Delete or Disable. 6. Navigate to My Catalog > My Listings. Confirm seller listings are active and correct. Turn off any unwanted 'buy' posts. 7. If the customer requests a refund and it meets policy, Click Raise Refund or Contact Billing Team. Note the refund reference ID and share ETA. 8. If the transaction is non-refundable or within policy limits, explain options clearly: use the single lead contact, or request support to escalate. 9. Offer immediate assistance: if the customer wants, arrange a callback from the packages team. Transfer the call or create a callback ticket. 10. Close with value add. Explain package benefits for sellers. Offer a short trial or a package demo to get daily leads.",
